  "interpretation": {
    "whatIsNewlySupported": [
      "All four successful CAS are bound to the same serving backend PID54 with distinct assigned XIDs11668\u201311671 and exact request revisions. Their actual raw projection/scope settings are NULL at the emitted records; no projection ON outcome is inferred.",
      "Across each before/after pair the retained backend context accounting rises by about6.4\u20136.5MB used. Later three after totals are33,250,768 /33,258,960 /33,291,920B, a small increase within this short case.",
      "The restore whole-group peak rises18,530,304B between two adjacent Node frames surrounding the RPC. Node endpoint RSS and heapUsed fall; cgroup anon rises while endpoint file/shmem are unchanged.",
      "The final peak is already recorded before attach, verifyLogical and finalRead frames; those later bounded frames do not set a higher retained group peak."
    ],
    "whatIsNotProven": [
      "Backend MemoryContext total/used/free are allocator accounting, not backend RSS/PSS, cgroup anon or whole-group charged memory. Unobserved allocations can peak outside the two snapshots.",
      "Memory context aggregation is a non-atomic traversal. The official SRF materializes a tuplestore and internally allocates context name/identifier text even though only scalar sums are exported. Both SRF and LOG instrumentation may alter the measured workload; no control arm quantifies their memory/CPU contribution.",
      "The interval also frees renderer_chunks and performs existing JSON uniqueness/size work. It adds output_text and output_value, but endpoint delta is a net lifetime difference plus observer effects, not the isolated cost of either representation.",
      "Output text length and JSONB pg_column_size are logical representation sizes; their sum must not be added to context totals, Node RSS or the cgroup peak. Similarity of net context growth to JSONB size is not allocation identity.",
      "Node heapUsed, heapTotal, external and RSS overlap. external includes arrayBuffers; file includes shmem and file_mapped is a subset/overlap. Separate maxima cannot be added, and endpoint current counters do not decompose historical peak.",
      "No same-instant process ownership was recorded at the parent peak. Endpoint Node RSS falling does not rule out a transient Node allocation or peak; rising group anon does not identify PostgreSQL rather than another owned process.",
      "Context count changing1744\u21922075 at before points and small byte drift do not establish retained objects, a leak, a long-run plateau or per-profile scaling.",
      "One CURRENT diagnostic with an observer ACL/logging exception is not a fair performance/RAM comparison and does not overturn historical W45 negative shared-memory evidence.",
      "The18,530,304B restore peak increment and6,416,800B restore net used-context change are overlapping observations and must never be added as distinct memory or savings."
    ]
  },
